#ZONE   INTERFACE   OPTIONS
#
# $NET_IF is the only interface. All of it is `net` by default; RFC 1918 ranges
# are carved out into `lan` via the hosts file.
#
# Options:
#   dhcp        allow DHCP client traffic (harmless if the address is static)
#   tcpflags    validate TCP flag combinations, drop illegal ones
#   nosmurfs    drop packets with a broadcast/multicast source
#   logmartians log martian (impossible) source addresses
#   routefilter enable reverse-path filtering (rp_filter)
#
net     $NET_IF   -    dhcp,tcpflags,nosmurfs,logmartians,routefilter
